% Modus tollens through a strict rule (VERIFY fixture for aida-strict-layer).
%
% tp argues P from a PRESUMED Q via the declared axiom pRule : Q->P.
% notP is a denied (strict) refutation of P.  Classically, refuting P
% refutes Q by contraposition of the rule, so Q must fall.
%
% Expected once the strict layer exists (the rule as its own strict edge,
% closed under transposition):
%   Q term OUT, Q context IN, P term OUT, P context IN.
% Today the rule is fused into the defeasible edge tp and no transposal is
% generated, so Q stays IN - the defect this fixture is meant to expose.
lk.
declare P,Q:bool.
declare pRule : (Q->P).
deny notP : (P).

start argument tp P
cut (Q->P) rule.
axiom pRule.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom rule.
end argument

start counterargument t P
moxia notP.
end counterargument

attack d t tp

graph d
label d
